body:
That's wrong, `get_rotation()` "doesn't account" for the full transformation. This will not work correctly e.g. for a `scale` like `(-1, 1)`. Example in action for the current state of the PR:

<img width="860" height="423" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95af4388-86b1-499f-8ee6-85b1242fd1f1" />

Besides that, `node->get_global_transform_with_canvas()` is only a part of the "to-screen" transform used above:
`Transform2D xform = canvas_item_editor->get_canvas_transform() * node->get_screen_transform();`

I'd change the code so it firstly maps the handle index to the local direction vector, then it remaps the direction vector to the screen space (using the same `xform` used for transforming the handles), and only then remaps the direction to a specific cursor shape.
